From: "Michael C. Pratt" <mcpratt@pm.me>
Date: Wed Sep 9 00:22:10 2026 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] generic: nvmem: u-boot-env: process numbered RADIOADDR variables

Similar to variable names with the pattern eth[0-9]addr,
some vendors have used variable names with the pattern RADIOADDR[0-9]
in order to store MAC addresses in the environment variables.
Because this variable name pattern is not documented,
processing them as binary addresses automatically
may not be upstreamable and the patch may need to be moved to hacks.

Signed-off-by: "Michael C. Pratt" <mcpratt@pm.me>
---

--- a/drivers/nvmem/layouts/u-boot-env.c
+++ b/drivers/nvmem/layouts/u-boot-env.c
@@ -108,6 +108,22 @@ static int u_boot_env_parse_cells(struct
 			info.read_post_process = u_boot_env_read_post_process_ethaddr;
 		}
 
+		/* Process RADIOADDR[0-9] variables as a MAC address. */
+		if (!strncmp(var, "RADIOADDR", 9) && isdigit(var[9]) &&
+		    strlen(var) == 10 && info.bytes == MAC_ADDR_STR_LEN) {
+			info.raw_len = strlen(value);
+			info.bytes = ETH_ALEN;
+			info.read_post_process = u_boot_env_read_post_process_ethaddr;
+		}
+		/* Handle quotation which increases length by 2 and offset by 1 if present. */
+		if (!strncmp(var, "RADIOADDR", 9) && isdigit(var[9]) &&
+		    strlen(var) == 10 && info.bytes == MAC_ADDR_STR_LEN + 2) {
+			info.offset = data_offset + value - data + 1;
+			info.raw_len = strlen(value);
+			info.bytes = ETH_ALEN;
+			info.read_post_process = u_boot_env_read_post_process_ethaddr;
+		}
+
 		nvmem_add_one_cell(nvmem, &info);
 	}
 
